ROSE uses EDG as a front-end to parsing C and C++.  We then read 
the EDG AST to generate the AST in ROSE using the Sage III IR.

New work, which is still ongoing, has implemented a newer interface
between EDG and ROSE and builds the AST via a more direct traversal
of the EDG source sequence lists.  This is likely an improvement over
the design which was based on a design closely followign the 
EDG unparser and build up the AST instead of generating code.  The
different design benifits from initial work by Jeramiah and permits
us to more readity use more current versions of EDG.  Originally
designed for EDG 3.10, it has been redesigned to support the EDG
version 4.0 interfaces (which is a much improved design over the 3.x
versions of EDG; simpler and easier to use).


*****************************************************
Notes specific to use of the EDG 4.x version in ROSE:
*****************************************************

   This implementation is represented in the edgRose directory.
This version is a refactored copy of the file new_sage_gen_be.C in 
the EDG_SAGE_Connection, which will be removed soon to reflect
the move to a new directory to better support the new interface 
work.

To use ROSE with the newer version of the EDG support uses the 
configure option: "--enable-edg-version=4.0"
Only the value of "4.0" is tested internally, but we should 
be able to handle "3.10" and soon "4.1".  Major and minor
version numbers are correctly identified.


*****************************************************
Notes specific to use of the EDG 3.3 version in ROSE:
*****************************************************

   This implementation is represented in the EDG_SAGE_Connection 
directory. We currently use version 3.3 of EDG (default), and although 
this has been robust and feature rich, we have some reasons for wanting 
to upgrade to later versions of EDG.

We use EDG mostly as is, and make only minor changes:
   1) Adding pointers to Sage III IR nodes to some structs in EDG (see il_def.h)
   2) We add the work to save literals as strings in the Sage III IR.

We need a more complete list, some of what has been modified in 3.3 is no longer required
in versions after 3.7. 

Newer work in 2009 added the ability to use EDG 4.0 to ROSE. This version will
also be patched to support the Nvidia EDG extensions required for CUDA support.


Old Notes:

1) To run the EDG unparser:
      $(ROSE_BUILD_TREE)/src/frontend/CxxFrontend/EDG/EDG_3.10/src/cp_gen_be --edg_base=$(ROSE_BUILD_TREE)/src/frontend/CxxFrontend/EDG/EDG_3.10/lib $(SOURCE_FILES)

   The --edg_base directory can also be set through the EDG_BASE environment variable.
   The output goes into <source-file-base-name>.int.c (even for C++).

2) New work in ROSE introduces a new connection between EDG and SageIII, the 
   new connection required a configure option "" 
   and also switches ROSe to use the EDG version 3.10 frontend.  This
   work is currently experimental and will evolve with time.


